1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:03,610
(Self-sufficiency)

2
00:00:03,610 --> 00:00:05,640
- It's good to see you again. - It's good to see you.

3
00:00:05,940 --> 00:00:07,840
Let's meet today's Rainbow Live guest.

4
00:00:07,840 --> 00:00:10,950
On stage, he shows an impressive performance.

5
00:00:10,950 --> 00:00:14,280
Off stage, fans love him for his unique sensibility.

6
00:00:14,450 --> 00:00:15,990
- It's DAWN! - DAWN.

7
00:00:15,990 --> 00:00:18,020
(Let us introduce DAWN.)

8
00:00:18,020 --> 00:00:19,190
DAWN.

9
00:00:19,190 --> 00:00:20,360
(Smiling)

10
00:00:22,060 --> 00:00:25,160
(He became known for his dreamy aesthetic.)

11
00:00:25,530 --> 00:00:26,800
("DAWN Builds His Own Musical World Through Songwriting and Producing")

12
00:00:26,800 --> 00:00:28,100
("All-Round Musician Who Has Written and Produced Since His Solo Debut")

13
00:00:28,500 --> 00:00:30,270
(He's a well-rounded artist who writes and produces his own music.)

14
00:00:30,670 --> 00:00:33,200
(A multi-talented musician, DAWN)

15
00:00:34,300 --> 00:00:35,640
(It's good to see you.)

16
00:00:35,740 --> 00:00:36,840
- Oh, gosh. - Oh, my.

17
00:00:37,310 --> 00:00:38,370
- Oh, gosh. - Oh, my.

18
00:00:39,240 --> 00:00:40,440
You little cutie.

19
00:00:41,310 --> 00:00:42,510
- Hi, cutie. - How adorable.

20
00:00:42,750 --> 00:00:44,050
You little cutie.

21
00:00:44,750 --> 00:00:45,980
- Hi, cutie. - How adorable.

22
00:00:46,620 --> 00:00:48,250
- Hi, puppy. - How cute.

23
00:00:48,250 --> 00:00:51,220
- No one has come with their dog. - Right.

24
00:00:51,220 --> 00:00:52,420
What's its name?

25
00:00:52,720 --> 00:00:54,360
Her name is Haetnim.

26
00:00:54,360 --> 00:00:55,760
- Haetnim. - She's a female dog.

27
00:00:56,430 --> 00:00:57,960
- She doesn't look nervous. - She's so well-behaved.

28
00:00:58,190 --> 00:00:59,860
- Is she always like that? - You little cutie.

29
00:00:59,860 --> 00:01:01,460
He loves having a dog around.

30
00:01:02,230 --> 00:01:04,100
- There you go again. - She's beautiful.

31
00:01:04,800 --> 00:01:06,040
- Sit. - Sit.

32
00:01:06,040 --> 00:01:07,300
- Sit. - Sit, Haetnim.

33
00:01:07,470 --> 00:01:09,270
There you go. You're amazing.

34
00:01:09,370 --> 00:01:10,470
Oh, yes.

35
00:01:10,470 --> 00:01:12,170
She seems to know her right side looks better on camera.

36
00:01:12,780 --> 00:01:15,040
- Always showing her right side. - Always showing her right side.

37
00:01:15,040 --> 00:01:17,080
- Please say hello to the viewers. - Sure.

38
00:01:17,450 --> 00:01:21,020
Hello, I'm DAWN.

39
00:01:21,220 --> 00:01:22,480
I do music.

40
00:01:22,480 --> 00:01:24,020
Awesome.

41
00:01:24,620 --> 00:01:27,520
DAWN is known for his aesthetics...

42
00:01:27,720 --> 00:01:30,360
- on social media. - Right.

43
00:01:30,790 --> 00:01:31,930
As far as I know, he loves...

44
00:01:31,930 --> 00:01:34,600
mixing unexpected pieces and has a thing for vintage items.

45
00:01:34,960 --> 00:01:36,070
He's so cool.

46
00:01:36,070 --> 00:01:39,870
- He's cool. - He's Hyun Moo's...

47
00:01:40,840 --> 00:01:43,840
- style icon. - Yes.

48
00:01:43,840 --> 00:01:45,410
- His fashion. - And style.

49
00:01:45,610 --> 00:01:48,380
- I have my own YouTube channel. - Okay.

50
00:01:48,510 --> 00:01:50,980
So many people mention Hyun Moo in the comments.

51
00:01:51,080 --> 00:01:52,150
- What? Why? - Why?

52
00:01:52,480 --> 00:01:55,180
"Hyun Moo would love this."

53
00:01:55,180 --> 00:01:57,650
"You should go on I Live Alone." There are so many comments.

54
00:01:57,650 --> 00:01:59,120
- So many people say that. - Really? Is your style aesthetic?

55
00:01:59,120 --> 00:02:00,190
(His heart is beating.)

56
00:02:00,390 --> 00:02:02,060
Please give me your number later.

57
00:02:02,260 --> 00:02:03,890
That's so sudden.

58
00:02:03,890 --> 00:02:05,130
That definitely got my attention.

59
00:02:06,100 --> 00:02:07,560
- He has great taste. - I need to learn from him.

60
00:02:07,800 --> 00:02:10,670
Let's take a look at his daily life.

61
00:02:10,670 --> 00:02:11,670
(Let's step into his daily life.)

62
00:02:12,770 --> 00:02:14,870
- How cute. - She's so well-behaved.

63
00:02:14,870 --> 00:02:16,070
- She's so calm. - She's so gentle.

64
00:02:16,070 --> 00:02:17,770
- You're adorable. - You can rest.

65
00:02:19,140 --> 00:02:23,010
(Slowly at DAWN's Own Pace)

66
00:02:23,610 --> 00:02:26,450
(A bright room with sunlight pouring in)

67
00:02:28,350 --> 00:02:30,450
You don't have blackout curtains?

68
00:02:30,850 --> 00:02:33,760
I like letting the sunlight wake me up naturally.

69
00:02:34,460 --> 00:02:36,090
I don't have curtains in my house.

70
00:02:39,030 --> 00:02:41,500
(Wriggling)

71
00:02:42,460 --> 00:02:44,430
(He wakes up naturally with the sunlight.)

72
00:02:44,430 --> 00:02:46,840
Hello, I'm Singer DAWN,

73
00:02:47,470 --> 00:02:50,910
and this is my fourth year living on my own.

74
00:02:52,980 --> 00:02:56,080
(I need to wake up quickly.)

75
00:02:58,010 --> 00:02:59,520
(Springing)

76
00:02:59,520 --> 00:03:01,980
- It's Haetnim we saw earlier. - It's Haetnim.

77
00:03:04,920 --> 00:03:06,160
How adorable.

78
00:03:06,160 --> 00:03:07,520
(Haetnim also woke up.)

79
00:03:10,290 --> 00:03:13,300
(Rolling)

80
00:03:14,430 --> 00:03:17,370
(He drags himself out of bed...)

81
00:03:18,070 --> 00:03:21,140
(and makes it first.)

82
00:03:22,040 --> 00:03:23,840
(Pulling up)

83
00:03:25,570 --> 00:03:27,510
(He raises the blind and opens the window to let some fresh air in.)

84
00:03:27,510 --> 00:03:29,550
You must air out the room.

85
00:03:31,680 --> 00:03:33,480
(Come here.)

86
00:03:34,320 --> 00:03:35,450
She's so cute.

87
00:03:36,080 --> 00:03:39,020
Her name is Haetnim.

88
00:03:39,390 --> 00:03:42,660
Was it 2019 or 2020?

89
00:03:42,660 --> 00:03:44,630
At first, someone I know...

90
00:03:44,630 --> 00:03:47,260
wanted to adopt a dog,

91
00:03:47,260 --> 00:03:49,230
preferably from a shelter.

92
00:03:49,900 --> 00:03:51,530
- So we went together. - Oh, my.

93
00:03:51,530 --> 00:03:54,200
- My gosh. - I fell in love with Haetnim...

94
00:03:54,470 --> 00:03:56,940
- and ended up coming home with her. - She looks happier now.

95
00:03:56,940 --> 00:03:59,070
- She looks more handsome. - Yes. She looks a lot better now.

96
00:03:59,710 --> 00:04:03,380
She's my soulmate.

97
00:04:03,380 --> 00:04:05,280
- You can tell her anything. - Yes.

98
00:04:06,880 --> 00:04:09,350
(He walks out of the room with his soulmate.)

99
00:04:09,720 --> 00:04:11,020
Well...

100
00:04:11,350 --> 00:04:12,920
(Clean)

101
00:04:12,920 --> 00:04:14,390
- It doesn't look like a house. - It's unique.

102
00:04:14,590 --> 00:04:17,260
- It's like an exhibit hall. - Yes, it's like an exhibit hall.

103
00:04:18,260 --> 00:04:20,900
(He walks across the exhibit hall...)

104
00:04:21,030 --> 00:04:24,130
(and opens the curtains.)

105
00:04:24,130 --> 00:04:26,000
- The windows are arched. - Arched windows?

106
00:04:26,000 --> 00:04:28,800
That's my dream window.

107
00:04:28,800 --> 00:04:29,910
(Shin Young's dream arched windows come into view.)

108
00:04:31,410 --> 00:04:33,910
(Relaxed)

109
00:04:35,710 --> 00:04:36,880
It was the second floor.

110
00:04:39,210 --> 00:04:42,850
It looks like it takes 30 seconds to come down the stairs.

111
00:04:44,150 --> 00:04:46,820
(He opens the curtains on the 1st floor as well.)

112
00:04:49,960 --> 00:04:51,830
- It's really interesting. - It's a nice place.

113
00:04:53,560 --> 00:04:55,600
It looks pretty.

114
00:04:55,600 --> 00:04:57,030
(Welcome to DAWN's tranquil house.)

115
00:04:57,700 --> 00:04:58,770
Oh, my.

116
00:04:59,600 --> 00:05:02,040
This is a two-story house.

117
00:05:02,040 --> 00:05:04,110
It's a house, not an apartment. That's my dream.

118
00:05:04,940 --> 00:05:07,640
I like preserving original features...

119
00:05:07,640 --> 00:05:09,610
instead of getting rid of them.

120
00:05:09,810 --> 00:05:12,750
I prefer working with what's already there.

121
00:05:14,050 --> 00:05:15,580
The first floor had wainscoting...

122
00:05:16,150 --> 00:05:19,550
on only one wall.

123
00:05:20,420 --> 00:05:24,390
So I wanted to mix in some Eastern-inspired pieces.

124
00:05:24,590 --> 00:05:27,830
That's why I filled the space with a lot of custom-made items.

125
00:05:27,830 --> 00:05:29,460
(A custom-made sofa set created to complement the space)

126
00:05:29,460 --> 00:05:31,170
- It's pretty. - What is that?

127
00:05:31,770 --> 00:05:33,000
Those were the kinds of things you'd see in a CEO's home...

128
00:05:33,000 --> 00:05:34,200
- back then. - I know. Back in the day.

129
00:05:34,200 --> 00:05:35,870
- The intertwined vines. - In the past... Yes.

130
00:05:35,870 --> 00:05:38,610
Do you know how much the table cost?

131
00:05:38,610 --> 00:05:39,980
- Okay. - Can you guess?

132
00:05:39,980 --> 00:05:41,310
- Shall we? - It must be quite expensive.

133
00:05:41,310 --> 00:05:42,610
Even a single branch...

134
00:05:42,610 --> 00:05:45,180
in my vivarium can cost around 100 to 200 dollars.

135
00:05:45,410 --> 00:05:46,580
How much is the table then?

136
00:05:46,580 --> 00:05:47,950
Isn't it over 10,000 dollars?

137
00:05:47,950 --> 00:05:49,150
It must be expensive.

138
00:05:49,280 --> 00:05:51,220
- It'd be around 15,000 dollars. - I think it's 20,000 dollars.

139
00:05:51,220 --> 00:05:52,720
- You think it's 20,000 dollars? - Yes, it's 20,000 dollars.

140
00:05:52,720 --> 00:05:54,790
It's 50 dollars.

141
00:05:55,820 --> 00:05:56,960
It's 50 dollars.

142
00:05:58,260 --> 00:06:00,330
- What, 50 dollars? - Hold on.

143
00:06:00,460 --> 00:06:01,600
Oh, boy. We were completely wrong.

144
00:06:01,860 --> 00:06:03,670
I spent ages searching for a table like that...

145
00:06:03,830 --> 00:06:06,300
- on secondhand apps. - You did?

146
00:06:06,540 --> 00:06:08,600
Then I found someone who was getting rid of one.

147
00:06:08,600 --> 00:06:09,970
- Yes. - I even brought it home myself...

148
00:06:09,970 --> 00:06:11,340
to save on delivery costs.

149
00:06:11,340 --> 00:06:12,810
The original price must've been pretty high, though.

150
00:06:12,810 --> 00:06:14,180
- It must've been expensive. - It was expensive.

151
00:06:14,180 --> 00:06:16,080
It must've cost a lot. The table ended up with the right person.

152
00:06:16,080 --> 00:06:17,780
- Right. - It looks amazing.

153
00:06:17,780 --> 00:06:19,480
- It looks so cool. - It's a really good one.

154
00:06:20,180 --> 00:06:22,480
Looking around, you'll notice objects...

155
00:06:22,720 --> 00:06:26,220
that reflect Korean culture.

156
00:06:26,420 --> 00:06:27,690
It's pretty.

157
00:06:27,820 --> 00:06:28,990
It's very unique.

158
00:06:28,990 --> 00:06:30,590
(DAWN has a unique and sophisticated taste.)

159
00:06:30,590 --> 00:06:31,730
What's this?

160
00:06:32,960 --> 00:06:35,200
(Immersed)

161
00:06:36,430 --> 00:06:37,900
It looks like he stole cultural treasures...

162
00:06:37,900 --> 00:06:39,370
- from all over the world. - I know.

163
00:06:41,540 --> 00:06:45,010
(Walking past the living room, you're greeted by a dining room...)

164
00:06:46,170 --> 00:06:47,810
(brimming with character.)

165
00:06:47,810 --> 00:06:50,310
The previous owner left that light fixture behind.

166
00:06:50,310 --> 00:06:51,380
What?

167
00:06:51,710 --> 00:06:53,820
- That's expensive. - Those are expensive in stores.

168
00:06:54,020 --> 00:06:55,020
- That one? - Yes.

169
00:06:55,020 --> 00:06:57,050
- No. That's from IKEA. - What?

170
00:06:57,790 --> 00:06:58,990
IKEA?

171
00:07:00,460 --> 00:07:03,130
(No way!)

172
00:07:04,130 --> 00:07:06,290
(I definitely bought out IKEA.)

173
00:07:07,600 --> 00:07:09,400
You went there. Why didn't you see that?

174
00:07:09,400 --> 00:07:10,730
Why couldn't you find an item like that?

175
00:07:11,570 --> 00:07:13,570
I'll make you one just by crumpling up some tissue paper.

176
00:07:14,400 --> 00:07:15,640
Yes. You're an artist too.

177
00:07:16,300 --> 00:07:18,270
(I'll make one for you.)

178
00:07:18,710 --> 00:07:20,640
(Past the IKEA lamp is a display cabinet.)

179
00:07:22,110 --> 00:07:24,780
My house is like a museum.

180
00:07:26,820 --> 00:07:29,550
(Heading upstairs from the museum-like 1st floor)

181
00:07:31,420 --> 00:07:33,120
(The interior takes a 180° turn.)

182
00:07:33,120 --> 00:07:34,720
It looks like a studio.

183
00:07:36,630 --> 00:07:40,000
- There's a sculptor I know. - Oh, my.

184
00:07:40,130 --> 00:07:41,660
That's the statue...

185
00:07:41,660 --> 00:07:43,600
I received as a gift.

186
00:07:44,730 --> 00:07:46,840
On the second floor, I just placed the things I love...

187
00:07:46,840 --> 00:07:49,740
without overthinking it.

188
00:07:49,870 --> 00:07:52,840
It brings back my dream of living in a house.

189
00:07:54,910 --> 00:07:56,410
(One wall features a painting he created himself.)

190
00:07:56,410 --> 00:07:57,910
- Do you paint too? - Yes.

191
00:07:57,910 --> 00:07:59,310
- I painted it. - You painted it?

192
00:07:59,310 --> 00:08:00,480
- Yes. - I thought it was done...

193
00:08:00,480 --> 00:08:01,680
by a professional artist.

194
00:08:01,680 --> 00:08:02,780
Me too.

195
00:08:02,880 --> 00:08:04,390
(Shy)

196
00:08:06,020 --> 00:08:09,190
(Sliding)

197
00:08:13,130 --> 00:08:17,130
(He calmly opens the windows and front door.)

198
00:08:19,630 --> 00:08:21,400
(It takes forever.)

199
00:08:23,370 --> 00:08:26,640
(Taking his time, he brushes his teeth, washes his face,)

200
00:08:30,150 --> 00:08:33,050
(and slathers on some lotion.)

201
00:08:37,690 --> 00:08:39,550
(Heave-ho)

202
00:08:42,460 --> 00:08:43,990
(Grabbing)

203
00:08:44,930 --> 00:08:46,830
(He takes out the ingredients without a second thought.)

204
00:08:47,630 --> 00:08:49,800
- What is he going to eat? - I'm so curious.

205
00:08:49,800 --> 00:08:50,830
(Curious)

206
00:08:55,870 --> 00:08:57,010
Cheese.

207
00:08:57,010 --> 00:08:58,970
(He took out cheese in the morning.)

208
00:08:59,810 --> 00:09:02,240
(Pressing)

209
00:09:03,950 --> 00:09:07,380
(Pressing again)

210
00:09:08,850 --> 00:09:10,190
It's not playing at half speed, is it?

211
00:09:11,250 --> 00:09:12,390
Was the knife dull?

212
00:09:14,560 --> 00:09:17,160
My nickname was Sloth.

213
00:09:20,130 --> 00:09:21,800
- Is that salami? - My goodness.

214
00:09:21,800 --> 00:09:23,730
(Taking his time, he slices the salami.)

215
00:09:25,170 --> 00:09:28,100
(Peaceful)

216
00:09:28,640 --> 00:09:30,370
I don't usually eat breakfast.

217
00:09:30,370 --> 00:09:32,070
I just drink coffee or tea.

218
00:09:32,910 --> 00:09:34,440
I put out some biscuits,

219
00:09:35,240 --> 00:09:38,510
- salami, cheese, and honey... - My goodness.

220
00:09:39,010 --> 00:09:41,750
to make an easy finger food platter.

221
00:09:41,750 --> 00:09:43,020
That's what I ate.

222
00:09:43,020 --> 00:09:44,020
(For breakfast, he has a simple finger food platter.)

223
00:09:44,020 --> 00:09:45,250
They go well with wine. Why is he eating them...

224
00:09:45,250 --> 00:09:46,490
- in the morning? - I know.

225
00:09:46,490 --> 00:09:47,520
- Those are for wine. - Wine.

226
00:09:47,520 --> 00:09:48,790
I love them.

227
00:09:52,190 --> 00:09:54,530
(He grabs a jar of honey.)

228
00:09:56,530 --> 00:10:00,040
(He takes out a big spoonful.)

229
00:10:01,640 --> 00:10:04,210
(The food is ready.)

230
00:10:07,840 --> 00:10:11,050
(He opens the fridge again.)

231
00:10:14,980 --> 00:10:17,220
- What? Are those soft drinks? - Soft drinks?

232
00:10:17,220 --> 00:10:18,890
(Why did he take out soft drinks?)

233
00:10:23,430 --> 00:10:25,330
- Black raspberry? - I see.

234
00:10:25,460 --> 00:10:27,430
It's good for stamina.

235
00:10:27,430 --> 00:10:28,430
(He pours it over black raspberry juice.)

236
00:10:29,600 --> 00:10:32,670
(He carefully pours the mixture into the glass.)

237
00:10:35,340 --> 00:10:37,610
(Satisfied)

238
00:10:39,670 --> 00:10:43,140
(He walks past the dining table.)

239
00:10:47,350 --> 00:10:49,550
(Plopping down)

240
00:10:53,120 --> 00:10:55,760
- My goodness. - Haetnim is next to him.

241
00:10:57,060 --> 00:10:58,060
(Right outside the front door)

242
00:10:58,060 --> 00:11:01,160
It has always been a dream of mine to own a yard even if it's small.

243
00:11:01,760 --> 00:11:02,830
It's my own yard.

244
00:11:02,830 --> 00:11:04,330
(The small-sized yard has been DAWN's dream.)

245
00:11:06,430 --> 00:11:08,870
(Chirping)

246
00:11:09,800 --> 00:11:11,070
Are birds chirping?

247
00:11:11,070 --> 00:11:12,810
- Are those actual sounds? - Yes.

248
00:11:13,640 --> 00:11:15,610
I think I turned on the background noise.

249
00:11:15,610 --> 00:11:16,850
Bird chirping sounds?

250
00:11:16,850 --> 00:11:17,850
(Come on...)

251
00:11:19,180 --> 00:11:21,480
(Playing the background noise)

252
00:11:22,720 --> 00:11:24,650
He is similar to me.

253
00:11:24,650 --> 00:11:26,220
- You always do the same. - Bird chirping sounds.

254
00:11:26,220 --> 00:11:27,290
- I always play them. - Same here.

255
00:11:27,290 --> 00:11:29,860
If you have a lot of grass in the yard,

256
00:11:29,860 --> 00:11:32,030
insects and mosquitoes enter the house.

257
00:11:32,130 --> 00:11:34,030
When insects enter the house...

258
00:11:34,500 --> 00:11:37,170
I don't catch any insects other than mosquitoes.

259
00:11:37,170 --> 00:11:39,470
- Same here! - Are you serious?

260
00:11:39,470 --> 00:11:40,570
- Really? - Yes!

261
00:11:40,570 --> 00:11:43,270
- Really? - I can't believe it.

262
00:11:47,940 --> 00:11:52,980
(He relaxes as he listens to the bird chirping sounds.)

263
00:11:55,650 --> 00:11:59,190
(Shall I eat now?)

264
00:11:59,920 --> 00:12:02,220
(Salty olives and cool black raspberry ade)

265
00:12:02,220 --> 00:12:03,790
I wanted a wine-like drink.

266
00:12:03,790 --> 00:12:04,930
- I see. - I see.

267
00:12:06,830 --> 00:12:08,560
- My goodness. - It's the Mediterranean.

268
00:12:08,560 --> 00:12:10,030
It feels like you're abroad.

269
00:12:10,030 --> 00:12:11,070
(The salami canapes suit the yard.)

270
00:12:12,700 --> 00:12:14,300
You put the food on the railing.

271
00:12:14,300 --> 00:12:15,570
- Yes. - I see.

272
00:12:15,570 --> 00:12:17,610
(He puts cheese on the cracker.)

273
00:12:19,270 --> 00:12:21,780
(Then he puts honey...)

274
00:12:21,780 --> 00:12:24,850
(and salami on the top.)

275
00:12:26,650 --> 00:12:29,450
(He puts the entire thing in his mouth.)

276
00:12:33,990 --> 00:12:35,990
(Patting)

277
00:12:36,930 --> 00:12:42,200
(Chewing)

278
00:12:42,200 --> 00:12:45,470
(Chewing)

279
00:12:51,040 --> 00:12:54,640
His eyes make me feel like he has no will to live.

280
00:12:54,640 --> 00:12:56,610
I know. It's like "The Last Leaf."

281
00:13:01,080 --> 00:13:02,650
I bet that drink goes well with the food.

282
00:13:02,650 --> 00:13:04,050
It's nice that he is so relaxed.

283
00:13:04,050 --> 00:13:06,250
(He tries a sip of black raspberry ade.)

284
00:13:09,460 --> 00:13:11,860
(Dazed)

285
00:13:11,860 --> 00:13:13,630
She has the same facial expression.

286
00:13:14,500 --> 00:13:15,830
- She resembles him. - How cute!

287
00:13:17,170 --> 00:13:18,400
She is so cute.

288
00:13:19,070 --> 00:13:20,070
(Wagging her tail)

289
00:13:20,070 --> 00:13:21,770
- She is so obedient. - She is like a human.

290
00:13:22,840 --> 00:13:24,710
Haetnim is hungry. That's right.

291
00:13:24,710 --> 00:13:26,410
- Oh, my. - She wants DAWN to share.

292
00:13:26,410 --> 00:13:27,640
"Give me my food."

293
00:13:28,080 --> 00:13:31,280
Haetnim has gained a lot of weight.

294
00:13:31,280 --> 00:13:33,250
- She doesn't look that way. - I feed her only at set times.

295
00:13:33,980 --> 00:13:35,020
Managing your dog's weight is important.

296
00:13:35,020 --> 00:13:36,350
- I need to manage her weight. - That's right.

297
00:13:42,660 --> 00:13:49,260
(He looks at the yard.)

298
00:13:50,900 --> 00:13:53,940
(Slouching)

299
00:13:56,870 --> 00:13:58,910
I always sit there.

300
00:13:59,070 --> 00:14:01,510
It's my favorite spot.

301
00:14:02,840 --> 00:14:06,550
Apparently, I have adrenal fatigue.

302
00:14:06,550 --> 00:14:07,850
I need a lot of sunlight.

303
00:14:09,650 --> 00:14:13,620
The big tree that's right in front of the spot is a magnolia tree.

304
00:14:14,690 --> 00:14:17,630
In spring, magnolias blossom.

305
00:14:17,760 --> 00:14:19,730
In winter, snow falls...

306
00:14:19,730 --> 00:14:21,160
and piles up...

307
00:14:21,160 --> 00:14:23,360
- on the branches. - Oh, my.

308
00:14:23,600 --> 00:14:24,630
He set up a tent in the yard.

309
00:14:24,900 --> 00:14:27,770
It's so nice. Haetnim always rests there too.

310
00:14:27,770 --> 00:14:29,340
(Haetnim also likes the yard.)

311
00:14:29,700 --> 00:14:33,340
I'm obsessed with the scenery.

312
00:14:36,580 --> 00:14:38,450
You don't take care of those weeds, right?

313
00:14:38,450 --> 00:14:40,480
No, I don't. They die in winter.

314
00:14:40,480 --> 00:14:41,520
That's it!

315
00:14:41,520 --> 00:14:43,890
(That's it!)

316
00:14:43,890 --> 00:14:46,190
- I also... - Stop saying you're the same.

317
00:14:46,190 --> 00:14:47,990
- Stop inserting yourself. - Seriously.

318
00:14:47,990 --> 00:14:49,560
- What is it this time? - I think...

319
00:14:49,560 --> 00:14:51,730
people who live in houses are divided into two types.

320
00:14:51,730 --> 00:14:52,830
You're nothing like him.

321
00:14:52,830 --> 00:14:55,230
They either manage the house meticulously or leave it be.

322
00:14:55,230 --> 00:14:56,830
- I'm totally the latter. - Only those two types...

323
00:14:56,830 --> 00:14:58,230
- live in a house. - Really?

324
00:14:58,230 --> 00:14:59,930
You leave it be as well, but it has different vibes.

325
00:14:59,930 --> 00:15:01,740
- Totally different vibes. - Your house is nothing like his.

326
00:15:02,470 --> 00:15:04,270
Your house is a bit different.

327
00:15:06,270 --> 00:15:08,980
(I enjoyed the food.)

328
00:15:11,250 --> 00:15:12,310
Shall we go inside?

329
00:15:14,480 --> 00:15:17,350
(Heave-ho)

330
00:15:18,850 --> 00:15:21,060
I'm so jealous that he lives in a house.

331
00:15:23,060 --> 00:15:27,160
(After breakfast, he gets changed in a relaxed way.)

332
00:15:28,600 --> 00:15:29,960
Okay.

333
00:15:31,570 --> 00:15:34,400
(Grabbing)

334
00:15:37,240 --> 00:15:40,340
(He grabs the notebook and walks over to the living room.)

335
00:15:40,980 --> 00:15:42,710
Okay. Let's go.

336
00:15:43,710 --> 00:15:45,650
- A timer? Does that mean... - A timer?

337
00:15:46,380 --> 00:15:48,950
(Okay. Let's go.)

338
00:15:54,760 --> 00:15:56,060
- Oh, my. - My goodness.

339
00:15:56,060 --> 00:15:57,590
You've changed a lot.

340
00:15:58,260 --> 00:15:59,560
What's this?

341
00:16:00,930 --> 00:16:04,530
This workout lets me finish everything in 30 minutes.

342
00:16:04,730 --> 00:16:06,600
It's the DAWN Challenge Workout.

343
00:16:06,770 --> 00:16:08,470
I start a stopwatch...

344
00:16:08,700 --> 00:16:10,810
and do a set per minute.

345
00:16:11,040 --> 00:16:13,110
After doing ten sets,

346
00:16:13,470 --> 00:16:14,940
I rest for ten minutes.

347
00:16:14,940 --> 00:16:16,080
A 10-minute rest after 1 set?

348
00:16:16,240 --> 00:16:19,180
I rest for 10 minutes. When I have 10 minutes rest,

349
00:16:19,280 --> 00:16:21,550
I do it again. So...

350
00:16:21,550 --> 00:16:22,920
I exercise for 20 minutes.

351
00:16:23,890 --> 00:16:24,920
It must be hard.

352
00:16:26,450 --> 00:16:28,960
(Shoulder tap push-ups)

353
00:16:30,930 --> 00:16:32,230
- What? - I can't believe it.

354
00:16:32,230 --> 00:16:34,460
- He must've done this many times. - He is so flexible.

355
00:16:36,000 --> 00:16:38,130
(He moves front and back once.)

356
00:16:40,470 --> 00:16:42,440
(After the squats, 1 set is done.)

357
00:16:42,440 --> 00:16:43,500
So that's one set.

358
00:16:43,500 --> 00:16:45,370
It's really hard to do one set.

359
00:16:45,370 --> 00:16:46,510
- It looks very hard. - Of course.

360
00:16:47,080 --> 00:16:49,040
(He catches his breath for a second.)

361
00:16:49,980 --> 00:16:52,910
(He starts the 2nd set right away.)

362
00:16:55,350 --> 00:16:58,250
(He does push-ups with shoulder and ankle taps.)

363
00:17:00,290 --> 00:17:04,190
(Then he continues with squats.)

364
00:17:04,990 --> 00:17:08,230
(After one set, he catches his breath again.)

365
00:17:09,930 --> 00:17:13,200
(Then he starts the 3rd set right away.)

366
00:17:13,700 --> 00:17:16,540
(Then comes the 4th set.)

367
00:17:16,540 --> 00:17:18,170
(Then comes the 5th set.)

368
00:17:18,970 --> 00:17:20,610
- Do you do ten sets? - Yes.

369
00:17:21,280 --> 00:17:22,340
That's intense.

370
00:17:23,210 --> 00:17:24,350
It's exhausting.

371
00:17:24,350 --> 00:17:25,780
It isn't easy to do that for 30 minutes.

372
00:17:29,520 --> 00:17:31,690
(He easily clears 10 sets.)

373
00:17:31,690 --> 00:17:32,690
How intense.

374
00:17:32,990 --> 00:17:34,160
All done.

375
00:17:36,490 --> 00:17:38,690
(Grabbing)

376
00:17:39,130 --> 00:17:40,360
(He sets up the mat as he catches his breath.)

377
00:17:40,360 --> 00:17:42,960
(What is he doing?)

378
00:17:54,510 --> 00:17:55,610
- Are you singing? - That came out of nowhere.

379
00:17:56,610 --> 00:17:59,580
(Why did he suddenly begin singing?)

380
00:17:59,580 --> 00:18:00,620
I do that...

381
00:18:00,920 --> 00:18:03,250
because I dance and sing on the stage.

382
00:18:03,750 --> 00:18:05,050
You want to improve your lung capacity.

383
00:18:07,720 --> 00:18:09,920
(My break is coming to an end.)

384
00:18:10,790 --> 00:18:11,860
(After checking the time)

385
00:18:11,860 --> 00:18:12,860
What next?

386
00:18:12,860 --> 00:18:14,160
(He gets ready for the next exercise.)

387
00:18:15,730 --> 00:18:16,800
Will he do jumps?

388
00:18:19,300 --> 00:18:20,370
Oh, my.

389
00:18:22,970 --> 00:18:24,440
(Sliding push-ups)

390
00:18:24,440 --> 00:18:26,210
You set up the mat for that.

391
00:18:27,480 --> 00:18:30,980
Kim Moo Yul's bodyweight workout with push-ups...

392
00:18:31,080 --> 00:18:32,810
was so cool.

393
00:18:33,410 --> 00:18:35,080
- That's right. - I see.

394
00:18:35,080 --> 00:18:36,280
(Moo Yul's push-ups made DAWN want to try them.)

395
00:18:36,650 --> 00:18:39,950
I wanted to try them, so I incorporated them into my workout.

396
00:18:41,460 --> 00:18:44,190
(He slides using the foot mat as support.)

397
00:18:45,930 --> 00:18:47,530
It has been two months since I began the challenge.

398
00:18:47,530 --> 00:18:49,300
Really? How can you do it so well in two months?

399
00:18:49,360 --> 00:18:51,470
- Push-ups are hard enough. - After ten sets...

400
00:18:53,530 --> 00:18:56,570
(He does 10 sets this time as well.)

401
00:18:56,570 --> 00:18:57,640
He has a strong core.

402
00:18:58,140 --> 00:18:59,640
He has a great core.

403
00:18:59,640 --> 00:19:01,240
(Grunting)

404
00:19:02,480 --> 00:19:05,110
(It's finally over.)

405
00:19:05,980 --> 00:19:07,550
(Panting)

406
00:19:07,550 --> 00:19:08,880
(Breathing out)

407
00:19:09,620 --> 00:19:10,620
Okay.

408
00:19:11,290 --> 00:19:12,350
Let's wash up now.

409
00:19:12,590 --> 00:19:13,590
It's so hot.

410
00:19:13,720 --> 00:19:16,420
(He goes to wash off his sweat.)

411
00:19:18,460 --> 00:19:21,430
(DAWN is done with his shower.)

412
00:19:21,430 --> 00:19:22,460
I feel so refreshed.

413
00:19:22,460 --> 00:19:25,130
(DAWN is done with his shower.)

414
00:19:25,730 --> 00:19:26,730
Okay.

415
00:19:27,640 --> 00:19:28,640
Haetnim.

416
00:19:30,940 --> 00:19:32,140
- My goodness. - There she comes.

417
00:19:32,140 --> 00:19:33,170
(She comes when her dad calls her.)

418
00:19:34,540 --> 00:19:35,580
Do you want to go for a walk?

419
00:19:36,440 --> 00:19:37,450
A walk?

420
00:19:38,380 --> 00:19:39,380
A walk?

421
00:19:39,380 --> 00:19:40,620
(Let's go right away.)

422
00:19:40,620 --> 00:19:42,750
A walk? Do you want to go for a walk?

423
00:19:43,250 --> 00:19:44,290
My goodness.

424
00:19:44,790 --> 00:19:46,720
- A walk? - She loves going for a walk.

425
00:19:47,790 --> 00:19:50,020
(You're so cute.)

426
00:19:51,390 --> 00:19:52,530
She is happy.

427
00:19:52,530 --> 00:19:53,660
(Haetnim doesn't mind having her face scrunched up.)

428
00:19:53,660 --> 00:19:54,730
Let's go.

429
00:19:55,960 --> 00:19:59,530
(Shall we get ready for a walk?)

430
00:20:00,940 --> 00:20:02,670
(She puts her head into the harness.)

431
00:20:03,870 --> 00:20:05,840
- Because she likes going out. - She's smart.

432
00:20:06,140 --> 00:20:07,310
She's very smart.

433
00:20:08,180 --> 00:20:10,680
(He heads outside with Haetnim into the warm sunshine.)

434
00:20:12,310 --> 00:20:14,520
(Slow)

435
00:20:16,120 --> 00:20:18,950
(Haetnim strolls along at a relaxed pace.)

436
00:20:19,920 --> 00:20:20,990
Hello.

437
00:20:23,160 --> 00:20:25,530
(He greets his neighbor and begins his walk.)

438
00:20:27,960 --> 00:20:29,960
Looking at him like this, you can really see his chest muscles.

439
00:20:29,960 --> 00:20:31,270
I haven't heard that word for a while.

440
00:20:31,830 --> 00:20:34,140
You're a former news anchor. You know that's slang for chest muscles.

441
00:20:35,940 --> 00:20:37,870
(He's striding while showing off his pecs.)

442
00:20:38,870 --> 00:20:41,310
Haetnim always does her business outside.

443
00:20:41,310 --> 00:20:43,740
So we need to go outside 3 to 4 times a day.

444
00:20:44,150 --> 00:20:47,550
We have several walking routes that we often take.

445
00:20:47,550 --> 00:20:50,250
There are about four for them.

446
00:20:51,420 --> 00:20:53,390
Does she not poop in the yard?

447
00:20:53,390 --> 00:20:55,460
She thinks it's part of her house.

448
00:20:58,230 --> 00:21:00,060
(I like being outside.)

449
00:21:01,130 --> 00:21:02,300
You're so good at doing your business.

450
00:21:03,400 --> 00:21:04,670
Good job.

451
00:21:04,670 --> 00:21:06,400
(Satisfied)

452
00:21:07,030 --> 00:21:08,840
(After they finished a refreshing walk)

453
00:21:08,840 --> 00:21:09,870
It's hot.

454
00:21:10,440 --> 00:21:12,910
(DAWN and Haetnim came home.)

455
00:21:13,710 --> 00:21:15,680
(He goes straight to the kitchen.)

456
00:21:20,410 --> 00:21:22,020
- Food for Haetnim? - Food for Haetnim?

457
00:21:23,350 --> 00:21:25,020
Food is ready. Come here.

458
00:21:26,390 --> 00:21:27,760
Is that raw meat?

459
00:21:28,060 --> 00:21:29,790
It's raw meat. I feed her raw food.

460
00:21:32,960 --> 00:21:34,500
It must be delicious.

461
00:21:34,500 --> 00:21:35,500
(Gobbling)

462
00:21:37,400 --> 00:21:41,040
(After feeding Haetnim, he goes to the dressing room.)

463
00:21:41,040 --> 00:21:43,500
(Rummaging)

464
00:21:45,470 --> 00:21:49,440
(He got changed and came out.)

465
00:21:51,010 --> 00:21:53,580
(He puts on long socks.)

466
00:21:53,580 --> 00:21:54,680
He's going somewhere.

467
00:21:57,180 --> 00:21:58,520
(He takes out his long boots and gets ready to go out.)

468
00:21:58,520 --> 00:22:00,350
- Long boots. It's summer. - Long boots?

469
00:22:00,620 --> 00:22:01,990
Right. But I like boots.

470
00:22:02,660 --> 00:22:03,790
Is he going to ride a motorcycle?

471
00:22:04,690 --> 00:22:06,090
Haetnim, see you later.

472
00:22:07,460 --> 00:22:09,930
Please behave. Don't cause trouble.

473
00:22:09,930 --> 00:22:12,370
(See you later.)

474
00:22:17,970 --> 00:22:19,140
Look at his chest muscles.

475
00:22:20,070 --> 00:22:21,780
- What? - All I can see are his pecs.

476
00:22:22,110 --> 00:22:23,210
DAWN's pecs.

477
00:22:23,610 --> 00:22:24,980
That's all I can see.

478
00:22:26,310 --> 00:22:27,380
There are shutters.

479
00:22:28,420 --> 00:22:30,120
- What? - Don't try to find a connection.

480
00:22:30,120 --> 00:22:31,690
There are shutters in my house too.

481
00:22:31,690 --> 00:22:33,690
(There are shutters in my house too.)

482
00:22:34,020 --> 00:22:35,920
- But you don't have chest muscles. - I don't.

483
00:22:36,320 --> 00:22:38,290
- If you don't, you're out. - Chest muscles.

484
00:22:38,590 --> 00:22:39,890
- You need pecs. - Your chest is just fat.

485
00:22:40,630 --> 00:22:41,930
He has muscles. You don't.

486
00:22:41,930 --> 00:22:42,960
Exactly.

487
00:22:43,430 --> 00:22:44,530
He's pure fat.

488
00:22:46,270 --> 00:22:48,470
(Getting closer)

489
00:22:51,540 --> 00:22:53,370
- That's an old car. - Yes, I drive an old car.

490
00:22:53,370 --> 00:22:55,080
- Is that a Volvo? - Yes, it's a Volvo.

491
00:22:57,080 --> 00:22:58,910
He's got great style.

492
00:22:58,910 --> 00:23:01,820
(It's parked in a small garage.)

493
00:23:02,620 --> 00:23:04,150
It's an old car.

494
00:23:04,490 --> 00:23:06,520
- It was manufactured in 1998. - In 1998?

495
00:23:06,520 --> 00:23:08,490
- In 1998? - That's what I'm talking about.

496
00:23:08,490 --> 00:23:10,260
- There's a cassette tape player. - A cassette tape player.

497
00:23:10,260 --> 00:23:11,460
You can't put a CD in there.

498
00:23:12,460 --> 00:23:15,630
I always wanted an old car.

499
00:23:16,400 --> 00:23:19,470
It cost 5,000 dollars. I named it Volduk.

500
00:23:19,970 --> 00:23:22,270
It has a name too. Because it's my first car.

501
00:23:22,640 --> 00:23:25,440
Nothing on this car is in good shape.

502
00:23:26,010 --> 00:23:27,110
That's cool too.

503
00:23:27,110 --> 00:23:29,710
If something breaks or falls off, I just tape it back on.

504
00:23:30,010 --> 00:23:31,750
I fix whatever I can myself and keep driving it.

505
00:23:31,750 --> 00:23:34,180
Everything falls off.

506
00:23:34,980 --> 00:23:36,780
Still, I like that car.

507
00:23:37,020 --> 00:23:38,050
Right.

508
00:23:38,820 --> 00:23:40,650
I paid 4,300 dollars for a car.

509
00:23:40,650 --> 00:23:41,660
- I paid 4,200 dollars. - No one will drive it anyway.

510
00:23:41,660 --> 00:23:42,720
I got it for similar reasons.

511
00:23:42,720 --> 00:23:44,890
There are so many camping cars,

512
00:23:44,890 --> 00:23:47,560
but I just wanted to get what I needed at a low price.

513
00:23:47,560 --> 00:23:48,960
- That's all I wanted. - Right.

514
00:23:48,960 --> 00:23:50,900
- I'm not really into cars. - Me neither.

515
00:23:51,130 --> 00:23:53,570
"Me neither?"

516
00:23:53,570 --> 00:23:55,500
- Stop saying, "I'm like that too." - That's enough.

517
00:23:55,500 --> 00:23:56,640
I'm going to get you for that.

518
00:23:56,640 --> 00:23:58,670
- "Me too. I'm like that too." - Don't try to make a connection.

519
00:23:58,670 --> 00:24:00,610
- You two are so different. - It's no joke, sir.

520
00:24:00,610 --> 00:24:01,680
Be quiet.

521
00:24:03,940 --> 00:24:05,980
(It starts with a key.)

522
00:24:05,980 --> 00:24:06,980
(Vroom)

523
00:24:06,980 --> 00:24:08,520
That's the beauty of an old car.

524
00:24:08,750 --> 00:24:09,880
You start it by turning the key.

525
00:24:09,920 --> 00:24:11,720
- Yes. It's not a smart key. - I haven't seen it for a long time.

526
00:24:11,720 --> 00:24:12,850
It's rare these days.

527
00:24:14,560 --> 00:24:20,460
(Setting off with Volduk)

528
00:24:21,230 --> 00:24:23,460
(Only silence)

529
00:24:23,460 --> 00:24:26,000
(Remains)

530
00:24:26,400 --> 00:24:28,540
(Only a sense of loneliness)

