01:07:11,410 --> 01:07:14,250
I don't know what you're going to add to that.

1566
01:07:15,350 --> 01:07:16,420
What is he going to make? Gosh.

1567
01:07:16,420 --> 01:07:18,550
The ingredients for my dish came from the site.

1568
01:07:19,860 --> 01:07:22,160
You shouldn't ask that.

1569
01:07:22,160 --> 01:07:23,430
Is that so? Okay.

1570
01:07:23,430 --> 01:07:25,730
You should just have those for now.

1571
01:07:27,500 --> 01:07:30,970
(Anxious)

1572
01:07:31,130 --> 01:07:33,670
Let's have the food the chief makes.

1573
01:07:34,140 --> 01:07:35,640
- Let's trust him. - Yes, let's trust him.

1574
01:07:35,710 --> 01:07:36,740
Let's wait and see.

1575
01:07:37,270 --> 01:07:40,810
(It'll be delicious.)

1576
01:07:41,010 --> 01:07:43,750
This is the dish I prepared.

1577
01:07:44,350 --> 01:07:47,150
If I were to describe it with my philosophy...

1578
01:07:50,090 --> 01:07:51,490
It's fine dump.

1579
01:07:51,990 --> 01:07:54,190
- Wait. Fine dump? - Gosh.

1580
01:07:54,190 --> 01:07:56,060
- What kind of fine dining is that? - I hate it.

1581
01:07:56,230 --> 01:07:58,330
- I won't hate it. - I hate the name itself.

1582
01:07:58,330 --> 01:08:00,060
- That's right. Dump is... - Fine dump?

1583
01:08:00,060 --> 01:08:02,060
- It sounds cool with "fine." - Fine dump.

1584
01:08:02,060 --> 01:08:04,070
I hate that it's dump.

1585
01:08:04,770 --> 01:08:06,170
You could've called it something else.

1586
01:08:06,170 --> 01:08:07,640
"Fine dining" and "find dump..."

1587
01:08:07,800 --> 01:08:09,170
are not that different.

1588
01:08:09,170 --> 01:08:10,870
- Gosh. - There's only a slight difference.

1589
01:08:10,870 --> 01:08:12,740
No, I hate that it's dump.

1590
01:08:12,740 --> 01:08:14,780
- But the way it looks... - I wonder how it tastes.

1591
01:08:14,780 --> 01:08:16,750
deserves its name.

1592
01:08:16,750 --> 01:08:18,410
You'll know if you watch it until the end.

1593
01:08:18,410 --> 01:08:19,880
- I'm curious. - Just watch until the end.

1594
01:08:20,750 --> 01:08:22,080
It's fine dump.

1595
01:08:22,890 --> 01:08:26,190
I added all the leftovers in the ramyeon pot.

1596
01:08:26,460 --> 01:08:29,230
That way, we can finish...

1597
01:08:29,230 --> 01:08:31,230
all the food we brought that day.

1598
01:08:31,730 --> 01:08:33,860
That was my philosophy. "Let's add all the leftovers."

1599
01:08:33,860 --> 01:08:35,030
(Fine dump dining dreams of a world with no leftover food.)

1600
01:08:36,770 --> 01:08:40,500
(He begins getting rid of all the leftovers.)

1601
01:08:40,500 --> 01:08:41,500
Let's add this.

1602
01:08:43,310 --> 01:08:45,370
You added instant rice without heating it, right?

1603
01:08:45,370 --> 01:08:47,410
- No, I didn't. - That way, the grains are firm.

1604
01:08:47,410 --> 01:08:49,110
- Is it like risotto? - That's right.

1605
01:08:49,110 --> 01:08:50,950
So far, it's ramyeon and rice.

1606
01:08:52,580 --> 01:08:53,620
Oh, dear...

1607
01:08:53,720 --> 01:08:55,220
- What is it? - Nothing.

1608
01:08:55,220 --> 01:08:56,250
(Grabbing)

1609
01:08:56,350 --> 01:08:58,350
It's not fine dump dining yet.

1610
01:08:58,350 --> 01:08:59,690
Oh, here it is.

1611
01:08:59,690 --> 01:09:01,090
(Adding the leftover pork slices)

1612
01:09:02,020 --> 01:09:03,190
That's how they fed dogs...

1613
01:09:03,190 --> 01:09:04,860
- in the countryside in the past. - That's right!

1614
01:09:04,860 --> 01:09:08,130
(That's how they fed dogs in the countryside in the past.)

1615
01:09:08,160 --> 01:09:10,170
- They had leftover jjigae too. - Dogs like them...

1616
01:09:10,170 --> 01:09:11,200
live healthy and long.

1617
01:09:11,200 --> 01:09:13,000
They lived long. You're right.

1618
01:09:13,170 --> 01:09:15,040
- They took so many nutrients. - That's right.

1619
01:09:15,170 --> 01:09:16,440
They didn't even need vaccinations.

1620
01:09:17,040 --> 01:09:19,240
You guys shouldn't get vaccinations either.

1621
01:09:20,240 --> 01:09:21,440
- We were... - What do you mean?

1622
01:09:21,440 --> 01:09:22,810
vaccinated by Kian84.

1623
01:09:22,810 --> 01:09:24,350
- Vaccinated by Kian84? - It's perfect.

1624
01:09:24,350 --> 01:09:25,620
- Great. - You got the primary vaccination.

1625
01:09:25,680 --> 01:09:27,220
You won't catch a cold in winter.

1626
01:09:27,220 --> 01:09:28,220
- Of course not. - Yes.

1627
01:09:28,220 --> 01:09:29,620
You won't catch a cold in winter.

1628
01:09:29,620 --> 01:09:30,890
- Of course not. - Yes.

1629
01:09:31,120 --> 01:09:33,390
Does that mean Kian84 is a germ?

1630
01:09:33,390 --> 01:09:34,420
Or virus.

1631
01:09:34,690 --> 01:09:37,260
- Your immunity will strengthen. - Ji Hyeon.

1632
01:09:37,260 --> 01:09:39,530
- Hold on, I've heard enough. - That's not what I meant.

1633
01:09:39,530 --> 01:09:41,160
- Virus! - Ji Hyeon!

1634
01:09:41,160 --> 01:09:42,600
- You're not wary of me at all! - Ji Hyeon.

1635
01:09:42,600 --> 01:09:44,500
- I mean... - Well done.

1636
01:09:45,030 --> 01:09:46,500
- He wasn't like this before. - Wait, this is...

1637
01:09:46,600 --> 01:09:48,770
- He's the best. - I mean, the logic is...

1638
01:09:49,270 --> 01:09:50,710
Ji Hyeon is... Gosh.

1639
01:09:51,240 --> 01:09:53,210
(He was just curious about the virus for the vaccination.)

1640
01:09:54,010 --> 01:09:55,580
(Dropping)

1641
01:09:56,650 --> 01:09:57,980
(Smiling)

1642
01:09:59,080 --> 01:10:00,350
- Why would you watch me? - No.

1643
01:10:00,350 --> 01:10:01,780
- I won't watch. - I just...

1644
01:10:01,780 --> 01:10:04,090
- I was just thinking. - It's not that bad.

1645
01:10:04,250 --> 01:10:06,160
(While MINHO is thinking...)

1646
01:10:06,560 --> 01:10:09,090
What? There's so much left.

1647
01:10:09,090 --> 01:10:10,560
(He adds kimchi calmly.)

1648
01:10:10,930 --> 01:10:14,730
- That's... - That's not a bad combination.

1649
01:10:14,900 --> 01:10:15,930
It's not bad.

1650
01:10:16,430 --> 01:10:17,900
(Rustling)

1651
01:10:18,870 --> 01:10:22,040
- Do you need garlic? - Oh, we had garlic too.

1652
01:10:22,040 --> 01:10:23,240
- There's Cheongyang chili too. - Good.

1653
01:10:23,240 --> 01:10:25,070
- That'd be really nice. - Oh, garlic?

1654
01:10:26,180 --> 01:10:27,680
It's a waste if we throw it.

1655
01:10:27,680 --> 01:10:29,680
Right. It's a waste.

1656
01:10:29,680 --> 01:10:32,010
He has a different perspective.

1657
01:10:32,080 --> 01:10:33,780
We have to throw it...

1658
01:10:34,150 --> 01:10:36,550
if we don't use it, so we must use it.

1659
01:10:36,550 --> 01:10:37,850
That's why the seasoning...

1660
01:10:37,850 --> 01:10:40,690
changes depending on how much food is left.

1661
01:10:40,690 --> 01:10:41,690
I see.

1662
01:10:43,460 --> 01:10:45,590
He hates wasting food.

1663
01:10:45,590 --> 01:10:47,100
- That's a good attitude. - Of course.

1664
01:10:47,560 --> 01:10:50,030
I gave a lot of thought into our crew's course.

1665
01:10:50,570 --> 01:10:54,040
I thought, "Should I try a city run that I haven't tried?"

1666
01:10:54,040 --> 01:10:55,200
That sounds fun too.

1667
01:10:55,200 --> 01:10:58,570
But there's this thing called shamanism running.

1668
01:10:59,140 --> 01:11:02,380
It's going to scary places where ghosts appear.

1669
01:11:02,850 --> 01:11:04,780
You have to run past a haunted house.

1670
01:11:04,910 --> 01:11:07,080
- It's a dawn run. - It's running in the mountains...

1671
01:11:07,080 --> 01:11:08,850
- past a haunted house. - It's so scary.

1672
01:11:09,120 --> 01:11:10,150
A graveyard run.

1673
01:11:11,050 --> 01:11:12,220
You get a crazy dopamine rush.

1674
01:11:12,220 --> 01:11:13,560
- You'll run like crazy. - And...

1675
01:11:13,860 --> 01:11:14,860
Our pace will go up.

1676
01:11:14,860 --> 01:11:16,860
Can't we do that first in summer?

1677
01:11:17,090 --> 01:11:18,260
Since it's summer now.

1678
01:11:18,260 --> 01:11:20,630
- I think... - I love them both.

1679
01:11:20,630 --> 01:11:22,700
- You'll run like crazy. - Our pace will go up.

1680
01:11:22,730 --> 01:11:24,670
- Actually, - Sounds interesting.

1681
01:11:25,070 --> 01:11:27,300
- a haunted house run is... - A haunted house run?

1682
01:11:27,300 --> 01:11:29,610
It's a little tough.

1683
01:11:30,110 --> 01:11:33,110
It's a big tough in a different way because of fear.

1684
01:11:33,110 --> 01:11:34,240
- You need to bet your life. - I...

1685
01:11:34,240 --> 01:11:36,910
don't know if I can say this,

1686
01:11:36,910 --> 01:11:38,380
but as the crew's training director,

1687
01:11:38,510 --> 01:11:40,550
- let me say something. - Sure.

1688
01:11:40,720 --> 01:11:42,620
I was a Marine who caught ghosts.

1689
01:11:42,790 --> 01:11:44,490
- It's so cool that he was a Marine. - Let's see if he doesn't scream.

1690
01:11:45,020 --> 01:11:46,690
- Gosh. - How charismatic.

1691
01:11:46,690 --> 01:11:48,290
(Dignified)

1692
01:11:49,430 --> 01:11:50,590
- He's so cool. - Wait.

1693
01:11:50,590 --> 01:11:54,900
(Marine MINHO's fighting spirit is surging at the mention of a ghost.)

1694
01:11:55,360 --> 01:11:56,830
(Happy)

1695
01:11:57,030 --> 01:11:58,830
(You were a Marine?)

1696
01:11:58,830 --> 01:12:00,000
I was a Marine who caught ghosts.

1697
01:12:00,000 --> 01:12:01,200
Auxiliary police officer Kian84.

1698
01:12:01,470 --> 01:12:03,510
You'd die too if a ghost appears, you punk.

1699
01:12:03,940 --> 01:12:06,410
That's what I wanted to say.

1700
01:12:06,480 --> 01:12:08,880
- Ghosts are really scary. - I have no problem.

1701
01:12:08,880 --> 01:12:10,280
- Seriously, I... - Ghosts are so scary.

1702
01:12:10,280 --> 01:12:11,980
I can take care of it.

1703
01:12:11,980 --> 01:12:13,020
- Really? - Yes.

1704
01:12:13,420 --> 01:12:15,990
I can see how MINHO would be 30 to 40 years later.

1705
01:12:15,990 --> 01:12:16,990
Seriously.

1706
01:12:17,250 --> 01:12:18,650
Me too.

1707
01:12:18,650 --> 01:12:21,260
- "Which batch were you in?" - "Which batch were you in?"

1708
01:12:21,890 --> 01:12:24,090
"You're so young, yet you can't run. Run!"

1709
01:12:24,230 --> 01:12:26,660
I'm so glad I wasn't born as his son or grandson.

1710
01:12:26,660 --> 01:12:28,560
I'd have been in trouble every holiday.

1711
01:12:28,560 --> 01:12:30,070
Let me add one more thing.

1712
01:12:30,070 --> 01:12:33,670
Not just anyone can take a photo in front of the First Division.

1713
01:12:33,670 --> 01:12:34,870
Oh, my gosh!

1714
01:12:35,340 --> 01:12:36,910
- Having that honor at that age... - A Marine...

1715
01:12:36,910 --> 01:12:38,770
- I got to because I won an award. - Really?

1716
01:12:38,770 --> 01:12:40,240
He's different.

1717
01:12:40,240 --> 01:12:42,110
I got a commendation from the division commander.

1718
01:12:42,110 --> 01:12:43,150
(The privilege of an award winner)

1719
01:12:43,450 --> 01:12:45,280
- It's scary. - I'm proud of him, though.

1720
01:12:45,280 --> 01:12:46,280
He's so cool.

1721
01:12:47,050 --> 01:12:48,050
I feel so proud.

1722
01:12:48,220 --> 01:12:50,090
(Fluttering)

1723
01:12:50,990 --> 01:12:51,990
That's right.

1724
01:12:51,990 --> 01:12:53,390
(Once a Marine, always a Marine.)

1725
01:12:54,060 --> 01:12:56,090
It smells delicious, though.

1726
01:12:56,090 --> 01:12:57,290
(While they were talking, the smell of ramyeon and rice spreads.)

1727
01:12:57,290 --> 01:12:58,430
It looks delicious.

1728
01:12:58,430 --> 01:13:00,430
- Gosh, the smell... - It looks delicious.

1729
01:13:01,060 --> 01:13:03,230
- Gosh. - The color doesn't look bad.

1730
01:13:03,230 --> 01:13:04,730
It smells amazing.

1731
01:13:04,730 --> 01:13:05,940
Nothing can beat this.

1732
01:13:06,100 --> 01:13:07,570
(Salivating)

1733
01:13:07,800 --> 01:13:08,840
Goodness.

1734
01:13:09,340 --> 01:13:11,210
It's totally Kian84's style.

1735
01:13:11,540 --> 01:13:13,580
Because it has garlic...

1736
01:13:14,410 --> 01:13:15,810
and kimchi...

1737
01:13:16,080 --> 01:13:17,710
It's refreshing.

1738
01:13:20,550 --> 01:13:22,120
As soon as he placed the pot,

1739
01:13:22,990 --> 01:13:24,050
I was surprised.

1740
01:13:24,850 --> 01:13:27,660
The visuals and the smell were crazy good.

1741
01:13:28,060 --> 01:13:29,290
"What is this?"

1742
01:13:29,290 --> 01:13:30,290
(He was excited at the unfamiliar smell.)

1743
01:13:30,290 --> 01:13:31,530
I was looking forward to it.

1744
01:13:31,560 --> 01:13:33,030
Yes, I wonder how it tastes.

1745
01:13:33,530 --> 01:13:35,300
- I think we'll finish it. - Yes.

1746
01:13:36,570 --> 01:13:38,200
- Try it. - Yes.

1747
01:13:38,200 --> 01:13:40,170
- Thank you for cooking. - Thank you for cooking.

1748
01:13:40,170 --> 01:13:41,870
Sorry. Let me take a photo.

1749
01:13:41,870 --> 01:13:42,970
Hurry up and take one.

1750
01:13:42,970 --> 01:13:43,970
(Halting)

1751
01:13:43,970 --> 01:13:45,570
Yes, let's take a photo.

1752
01:13:46,410 --> 01:13:47,640
(Click)

1753
01:13:48,440 --> 01:13:50,680
- Yes, let's take a photo. - You're the first ones...

1754
01:13:50,680 --> 01:13:51,780
to take a photo of my food.

1755
01:13:53,180 --> 01:13:55,780
(Emotional)

1756
01:13:55,780 --> 01:13:58,150
I'll take a photo of you two. Get closer.

1757
01:13:59,290 --> 01:14:01,660
You're the first ones to take a photo of my food.

1758
01:14:01,920 --> 01:14:03,990
Others were disgusted by his food.

1759
01:14:05,190 --> 01:14:07,730
Why are you crying?

1760
01:14:07,830 --> 01:14:09,430
It looks great too.

1761
01:14:09,430 --> 01:14:10,970
It looks delicious. What's wrong?

1762
01:14:10,970 --> 01:14:12,100
I can't believe you took a photo of it.

1763
01:14:13,000 --> 01:14:14,070
Thank you.

1764
01:14:14,140 --> 01:14:15,810
- Kian84 was really moved. - I know.

1765
01:14:16,510 --> 01:14:18,140
My food has always been looked down on.

1766
01:14:20,080 --> 01:14:21,540
(Moved)

1767
01:14:21,540 --> 01:14:22,950
- Thank you for this. - Help yourself.

1768
01:14:23,680 --> 01:14:25,310
It was...

1769
01:14:26,050 --> 01:14:27,680
I was grateful.

1770
01:14:27,950 --> 01:14:29,050
- He's broken. - He's broken.

1771
01:14:29,050 --> 01:14:31,750
There was no one...

1772
01:14:33,220 --> 01:14:35,060
who took a photo of my food.

1773
01:14:36,060 --> 01:14:37,560
I almost cried then.

1774
01:14:38,560 --> 01:14:40,000
You were really emotional.

1775
01:14:40,000 --> 01:14:42,360
I guess I've felt upset all along.

1776
01:14:42,360 --> 01:14:44,730
They'd be like, "Why do you eat like such food?"

1777
01:14:44,730 --> 01:14:46,600
I guess it was bottled up without me knowing.

1778
01:14:46,600 --> 01:14:47,670
You must've been upset.

1779
01:14:48,440 --> 01:14:51,670
(The photo Na Ra took, the photo MINHO took)

1780
01:14:51,670 --> 01:14:54,480
I don't know why they took a photo of that.

1781
01:14:55,410 --> 01:14:58,150
Honestly, I don't like it when people take a photo of food.

1782
01:14:58,680 --> 01:15:00,780
I'd be like, "You'll eat them up anyway. Why bother taking a photo?"

1783
01:15:01,820 --> 01:15:04,120
But they took a photo of it as though a chef made it.

1784
01:15:05,820 --> 01:15:07,190
I was grateful for that.

1785
01:15:07,320 --> 01:15:09,060
They're such good friends.

1786
01:15:10,060 --> 01:15:11,090
Thank you.

1787
01:15:11,090 --> 01:15:14,160
(Touched)

1788
01:15:14,500 --> 01:15:16,370
I had too much noodles earlier,

1789
01:15:16,370 --> 01:15:17,900
- so I should have rice now. - I know.

1790
01:15:17,900 --> 01:15:19,200
(They finally try it after taking photos.)

1791
01:15:20,740 --> 01:15:23,210
- After tasting it... - I bet it's good.

1792
01:15:23,210 --> 01:15:24,610
(Expectant)

1793
01:15:28,580 --> 01:15:29,950
- Are you satisfied with it? - Is it okay?

1794
01:15:30,210 --> 01:15:31,250
Isn't it a bit bland?

1795
01:15:31,810 --> 01:15:33,250
It's okay. It's not bad.

1796
01:15:33,520 --> 01:15:35,680
It must be good.

1797
01:15:36,290 --> 01:15:38,450
(Na Ra takes a bite too.)

1798
01:15:38,450 --> 01:15:39,790
(Exclaiming)

1799
01:15:40,960 --> 01:15:42,420
- You guys... - It's delicious.

1800
01:15:43,130 --> 01:15:44,730
- It's delicious. - Seriously...

1801
01:15:45,260 --> 01:15:46,430
Eat your fill, guys.

1802
01:15:49,000 --> 01:15:51,400
What's the closest food you can describe it to?

1803
01:15:51,400 --> 01:15:52,640
- Budae jjigae? - Budae jjigae?

1804
01:15:52,640 --> 01:15:54,770
At first, it tasted like omori kimchi jjigae.

1805
01:15:54,770 --> 01:15:56,310
- Oh, omori kimchi jjigae? - That's right.

1806
01:15:56,640 --> 01:15:58,070
- Was the kimchi aged? - Aged kimchi.

1807
01:15:58,110 --> 01:15:59,710
- Like aged kimchi jjigae. - I'm even more grateful...

1808
01:15:59,710 --> 01:16:01,780
that you called it omori.

1809
01:16:01,780 --> 01:16:03,910
(Moved)

1810
01:16:04,310 --> 01:16:06,980
(Slurping)

1811
01:16:08,350 --> 01:16:10,550
(MINHO inhales everything.)

1812
01:16:10,550 --> 01:16:11,620
It was really good.

1813
01:16:11,620 --> 01:16:12,890
- It was so good... - I know.

1814
01:16:12,890 --> 01:16:14,360
- You're eating from the bowl. - that I'm salivating even now.

1815
01:16:14,360 --> 01:16:15,360
- Really? - Yes.

1816
01:16:15,360 --> 01:16:16,360
(Gulping)

1817
01:16:17,960 --> 01:16:21,260
(Na Ra enjoys the ramyeon and rice too.)

1818
01:16:23,200 --> 01:16:25,970
I wanted to try the food that Kian84 cooked.

1819
01:16:26,870 --> 01:16:27,970
